Frozen for RFC 0132 (ar-closure-assertion-parity).

Its stories converge assertions file by file inside one package, and every one
of them would otherwise rewrite the same three activerecord counters — which
serializes the whole RFC on this file. The mark only shrinks, so leaving it
untouched while the counters fall is green the whole way; the RFC's closing
story `tighten-assertion-mark-after-0132` deletes this marker and reseeds once.

Until then the ratchet is not ENFORCING on the ground already converged: a
regression inside the accumulated slack does not fail the gate. It is not
silent — every gate run over a complete artifact prints the slack per package,
failing runs included, and those numbers should only ever fall. Do not widen the scope of this freeze, and do not add a second
campaign to it.
